        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "4000f0c5-1f0e-5ac0-9e5a-6a930824d7ec",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: One Big Hapa Family, A Film Unfinished, Das Ghetto\n- People: Jeff Chiba Stearns, Yael Hersonski\n- Places: Warsaw Ghetto\n- Concepts: Grossaktion Warsaw, German propaganda film\n\nFacts:\n- In 1942, the German propaganda film Das Ghetto was made to depict the Warsaw Ghetto two months before the mass extermination of its inhabitants during Grossaktion Warsaw.\n- In 2010, One Big Hapa Family was released as an animated/live-action documentary film directed by Canadian director Jeff Chiba Stearns.\n- In 2010, Yael Hersonski released A Film Unfinished, a documentary film also known by the Hebrew title Shtikat haArkhion and the German title Geheimsache Ghettofilm.\n- A Film Unfinished re-examines the making of the unfinished 1942 German propaganda film Das Ghetto.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "70b97038-d647-51d2-a294-ab4fdad4076a",
        "text": "Page: One Big Hapa Family. Sentence: One Big Hapa Family is a 2010 animated/live-action documentary film directed by Canadian director Jeff Chiba Stearns.\nPage: A Film Unfinished. Sentence: A Film Unfinished (Hebrew title: \"שתיקת הארכיון\" \"Shtikat haArkhion\", German title: \"Geheimsache Ghettofilm\") is a 2010 documentary film by Yael Hersonski, which re-examines the making of an unfinished 1942 German propaganda film (titled \"Das Ghetto\", \"The Ghetto\") depicting the Warsaw Ghetto two months before the mass extermination of its inhabitants in the German operation known as the Grossaktion Warsaw.",
